<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Italica</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Italica was a Roman city near modern Santiponce, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scipio-africanus">Scipio Africanus</a> in 206 BCE for wounded veterans of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>. It was the birthplace of the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a> and probably of Hadrian, who enlarged it with a new quarter, and its amphitheatre was one of the largest in the Roman world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/italica.jpg" alt="Italica" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ColdEel · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Italica_schema.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
